ssharcade router (ssh-arcadelobby)
==================================

Third-party software distributed in the published container image
(ghcr.io/mynameis-nigel/ssh-arcadelobby).

ssh-arcadelobby itself is MIT-licensed; see LICENSE. The entries below cover
software redistributed *inside the image*, rather than depended on as source.


Litestream
----------

  Version:  0.5.12  (pinned in Dockerfile)
  Source:   https://github.com/benbjohnson/litestream
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0
            https://github.com/benbjohnson/litestream/blob/main/LICENSE

Used as the replication process that supervises the router binary. Copied
into the image as a prebuilt static binary from litestream/litestream:0.5.12,
unmodified. It is a separate program run as the container's supervising
process, not linked into this program's code.

Apache-2.0 section 4 requires this attribution to travel with the binary,
which is why this file exists even though none of this repository's own code
is Apache-licensed.


Go module dependencies
----------------------

Every Go dependency is permissive (MIT or BSD-3-Clause) and is compiled into
the binary rather than redistributed as a separate work. See go.mod for the
list, and each module's own repository for its licence text.


Base image
----------

The runtime is alpine:3.22 plus ca-certificates. Packages arriving with the
base image are covered by their own licences as published by Alpine Linux
(https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org) and are not enumerated here — the same scope
boundary ssh-chess's NOTICE draws.
